! ===================================================================
! Mac-style modifier swap (physical Win <-> Ctrl), for alitoh's i3 box.
!
! Goal: on macOS the big "command" modifier lives where the Win key is
! on a PC keyboard (thumb key, next to the space bar). Linux puts app
! shortcuts (copy/paste/close/save) on Ctrl, and i3 puts its WM mod on
! Win (Mod4). This swaps them so muscle memory from a Mac feels right:
!
!   physical Win  -> emits Control  (so Win+C = copy, Win+W = close, etc.)
!   physical Ctrl -> emits Super    (Mod4)  -> becomes the i3 mod key
!
! Consequences after this map is active:
!   * App shortcuts (Ctrl+*): press the physical *Win* key.
!   * i3 shortcuts (Mod4+*):   press the physical *Ctrl* key.
!
! To revert / disable: delete ~/.Xmodmap (or the line loading it in
! ~/.xprofile) and log out/in. Nothing here is permanent.
! ===================================================================

remove Control = Control_L Control_R
remove Mod4    = Super_L Super_R

keycode  37 = Super_L      ! physical Left Ctrl  -> Super (i3 mod / Mod4)
keycode 133 = Control_L    ! physical Left Win   -> Control (Mac-style Cmd)
keycode 105 = Super_R      ! physical Right Ctrl -> Super
keycode 134 = Control_R    ! physical Right Win  -> Control

add Control = Control_L Control_R
add Mod4    = Super_L Super_R
